{"name":"Roman Empire Red","hex":"#ee1111","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Upright, as opposed to italic.","Of or related to the Latin alphabet or roman numerals."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the main three types used for the Latin alphabet (the others being italics and blackletter), in which the ascenders are mostly straight.","Ellipsis of roman numeral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roman"},{"term":"empire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A political state, often a monarchy, that has achieved a much greater current size than its initial size by conquering surrounding territories, cities or nations.","A political unit ruled by an emperor or empress."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Empire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empire"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roman Empire","blocks":[{"text":"The Roman Empire was a state that dominated the Mediterranean and much of Europe, Western Asia, and North Africa during the classical period. The Roman Republic had previously conquered most of these territories, which later came under permanent single-person rule following Octavian's rise to power and the establishment of the Augustan Principate in 27 BC. By the late 3rd century AD, the empire had been divided many times. The Western Roman Empire collapsed in 476 AD, whereas the Eastern Roman Empire persisted until the fall of Constantinople in 1453."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Roman_Empire_Trajan_117AD.png/330px-Roman_Empire_Trajan_117AD.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire"},{"title":"Empire","blocks":[{"text":"An empire is a group of territories controlled by a monarch or a supreme central authority. Within an empire, different populations may have different sets of rights and may be governed differently. The word \"empire\" derives from the Roman concept of Imperium, which refers to the right to command. Empires have taken many forms throughout history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Modern_Empires.svg/330px-Modern_Empires.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Augustus_of_Prima_Porta_%28inv._2290%29.jpg/500px-Augustus_of_Prima_Porta_%28inv._2290%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.w